# Websocket frame corruption fix (0151): the 0144 mongoose 7.14 upgrade
# dropped the old global mongoose_lock, and this port runs every kiwi task as
# a real pthread (support/coroutines.cpp) — send_msg*() from task threads
# raced the web server task's poll-side socket write on mc->send, producing
# malformed frames (zeroed/misaligned headers) and probabilistic /admin
# disconnects. Routes send_msg_buf()/send_msg_mc() through the locked s2c
# nbuf queue so only the poll thread calls mg_ws_send().
# Verified with -F 0 against the full post-0019 series tree.
0151-websocket-send-via-s2c-queue.patch
# Websocket control messages must not be dropped (0152): 0151 routed
# send_msg*() through the s2c nbuf queue whose stream-data watermarks
# (ND_HIWAT=64 ovfl latch) silently dropped the /admin startup burst's
# ext_call extension-config messages -> Extensions tab lost all extensions
# except ant_switch. Adds nbuf_allocq_critical() (bypasses ovfl, pathological
# 1024-entry cap only) used by send_msg_buf()/send_msg_mc(); stream audio/WF
# data keeps the original drop behaviour.
# Verified with -F 0 against the full post-0151 series tree.
0152-websocket-control-msgs-no-drop.patch

# 0020: kiwi_str_encode (support/str.cpp) — mongoose mg_url_encode() does
# NOT percent-encode '%' itself, so console output containing '%' (e.g.
# ping's "0% packet loss") went onto the websocket with a raw '%' and broke
# the client's decodeURIComponent. Expand '%' -> '%25' after mg_url_encode.
0020-encode-percent-in-kiwi-str-encode.patch

# 0021: kiwi_decodeURIComponent (web/kiwi/kiwi_util.js) — the recovery loop
# that strips invalid %xx sequences only set double_fail when it actually
# removed something; a payload whose only flaw was a bare '%' (from the
# 0020 bug) removed nothing and the while(obj==null) loop spun forever,
# freezing the browser tab at 100% CPU. Track a `removed` flag and force
# double_fail when nothing was removed.
0021-decodeURIComponent-infinite-loop.patch
